Alternative concept: Comparable
Comparable<Team> can be implemented inside the Team class using compareTo(). It defines the team's natural ranking order.
A Comparator is more flexible because different ranking rules can be created without changing the Team class.
Conclusion
The generic Leaderboard<T> can work with different object types. Comparator provides flexible ranking based on multiple fields, while sorting a copy preserves the original list.
